# ChangeLog

## 2026-10-17

- Reworked the single-page landing page with Turkish and English content, an accessible language toggle, clearer calls to action, and a consolidated PlusClouds banner.
- Added search description and Open Graph metadata, a theme color, and a favicon.
- Disabled video autoplay, added playback guidance, and enabled lazy loading for the YouTube iframe.
- Updated the responsive layout and added a visible hover and keyboard-focus color for the PlusClouds banner.
- Added the complete AGPL-3.0-or-later notice as a source comment to project-owned HTML, JavaScript, CSS, SVG, Python, workflow, and server configuration files.
- Generated a 240-pixel WebP display logo and a 64-pixel PNG favicon from the existing logo artwork while preserving the original SVG files. The display asset is about 96% smaller than the minified SVG.
- Added LiteSpeed/Apache response headers in `.htaccess` for Content Security Policy, HSTS, MIME sniffing protection, framing, referrer behavior, and browser feature permissions. Documented the requirements for enabling the configuration and verifying headers after deployment.
- Added a dependency-free Python validation script for document structure, local assets, accessibility labels, iframe loading, external-link safety, and SVG parsing.
- Added a GitHub Actions workflow to run the site checks on pushes and pull requests.
- Added "Source Code" and "JS Code" links to the footer, translated with the Turkish and English language toggle. The source link points to the project repository, and the JS link opens the site's `app.js` file directly in the browser.
- Declared JavaScript files as UTF-8 in `.htaccess` so Turkish text displays correctly when `app.js` is opened directly from either language view. A live check showed the server still sent `Content-Type: text/javascript` without a charset, so the setting takes effect only after this change is deployed.
- Added a UTF-8 byte order mark to `app.js` so browsers detect the encoding even when the server does not send a charset. The Turkish strings remain written with the Turkish alphabet (ş, ı, ğ, ö, ü, ç) rather than `\u` escapes.
- Corrected Turkish copy: "işbirliği" is now "iş birliği", "resmi" is now "resmî", and the footer link "Kaynak Kod" is now "Kaynak Kodu".
- Rewrote the README in US English with feature, preview, validation, hosting, license, and recent-change information.
